    },
    {
      "category": "overview",
      "field": "paradigm_case",
      "value": "The paradigm case of a crime lies in the proof, beyond reasonable doubt, that a person is guilty of two things: the accused must commit an act which is deemed by society to be criminal (actus reus) and have the requisite malicious intent to do a criminal act (mens rea).",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "source": null,
      "metadata": {
