    },
    {
      "category": "overview",
      "field": "intention_and_negligence",
      "value": "Criminal systems of the civil law tradition distinguish between intention (dolus directus and dolus eventualis) and negligence, which does not carry criminal responsibility unless a specific crime provides for its punishment.",
